{%- comment -%}
  Returns · delivery by region — its own section so it can sit last on
  the product page, just above the footer (owner's direction, Sep 2026).
  Styles are in assets/sv-product.css §21 (loaded by sv-product, which
  is always on this template). The delivery zones are this section's
  blocks; shop metafields override them where they exist.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="sv-pdp-facts" data-sv>
  <div class="w">
      <div class="sv-pdp__facts sv-pdp__facts--row">

        {%- comment -%}
          ── Delivery ─────────────────────────────────────────
          ARCHITECTURE §6.8 element 8 asks for a date rather than a
          duration. It cannot honestly be one here, for two reasons
          found in the live store: Liquid has no access to the
          visitor's state, so any single date would be a guess at
          which zone they are in; and the published Shipping Policy
          says in terms "we are not able to guarantee a delivery
          date". So: the dispatch promise, which IS a commitment,
          from its shop metafield — then the zones, named.

          Zone figures come from shop metafields where they exist and
          from the section's own blocks otherwise. There is no
          `default:` filter anywhere below, and no figure is written
          into this template: a default is a hard-coded business
          value in disguise and keeps rendering the stale number
          after Admin is corrected (sv-credentials.liquid).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'sv-returns-line', class: 'sv-pdp__fact', show_label: true -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The dispatch promise is a tile above, so this is the detail
          behind it: per-zone time and charge. A <details> because the
          headline fact is already standing open; this is lookup.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <details class="sv-pdp__exp sv-pdp__fact" open>
          <summary>Delivery time and charges by region</summary>
          <div class="sv-pdp__expbody">
          <p class="sv-pdp__factbody">Delivery is counted from dispatch, not from the day you order.</p>

          {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
            <ul class="sv-pdp__zones" role="list">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type != 'zone' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign days = block.settings.days
                  assign charge_rupees = block.settings.charge

                  # Shop metafields win where they exist — the business
                  # constants layer is the source of truth, and these
                  # blocks are the stand-in until it is complete.
                  assign days_key = 'delivery_days_' | append: block.settings.metafield_key
                  assign charge_key = 'delivery_charge_' | append: block.settings.metafield_key
                  assign mf_days = shop.metafields.custom[days_key].value
                  assign mf_charge = shop.metafields.custom[charge_key].value
                  if mf_days != blank
                    assign days = mf_days
                  endif
                  if mf_charge != blank
                    assign charge_rupees = mf_charge
                  endif

                  # Both sources hold rupees as a number, so the symbol
                  # comes from Shopify's currency formatting and a typed
                  # "₹" never appears anywhere in the theme.
                  assign charge = ''
                  if charge_rupees != blank
                    assign charge = charge_rupees | times: 100 | round | money_without_trailing_zeros
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- if block.settings.name != blank and days != blank -%}
                  <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="sv-pdp__zonename">{{ block.settings.name }}</span>
                    <span class="sv-pdp__zonedays">{{ days }}</span>
                    {%- if charge != blank -%}<span class="sv-pdp__zonecost">{{ charge }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The free-delivery threshold, from the one metafield that
            already holds it. sv-announcement-line.liquid documents
            the shape: a `money` metafield's .value is already in the
            subunit, so the money filter takes it raw.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Returns & delivery",
  "tag": "div",
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["product"] },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Delivery zones show beside the returns policy. Where the matching shop metafield exists (custom.delivery_days_kerala, custom.delivery_charge_kerala and so on) it overrides what is typed here, so Admin stays the source of truth."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "zone",
      "name": "Delivery zone",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Zone", "info": "As it reads to a customer, e.g. Kerala" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "days", "label": "Delivery time", "info": "Counted from dispatch, e.g. 2 to 4 working days" },
        { "type": "number", "id": "charge", "label": "Shipping charge, in rupees", "info": "Digits only — the currency symbol comes from Shopify's own formatting. Leave empty to show the zone without a price." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "metafield_key",
          "label": "Shop metafield to read instead",
          "options": [
            { "value": "kerala", "label": "Kerala" },
            { "value": "south", "label": "South India" },
            { "value": "rest", "label": "Rest of India" },
            { "value": "remote", "label": "Remote areas" }
          ],
          "default": "kerala"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "SV Returns & delivery" }]
}
{% endschema %}
